  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader who uses the largest Dynamic Type sizes, I want the Messages, topic list, Favoris and reader headers to stay readable at « Accessibilité – XL », so that a row is not one word per line and no label is clipped.\n\nFound by the Mac pass of #693 (iPhone 18 Pro, iOS 27.2, dev-swift @ 9f7ec2b8, `xcrun simctl ui … content_size accessibility-extra-large`, light and dark alike). Not checked against legacy at that size: the legacy layout at the same size is the reference to read before fixing.\n\n### What happens\n1. **Messages row** (`MessageRowView`): the « non lu » capsule, the avatar and the unread dot leave a column of about 300 px for the title, which wraps one word per line (a title of three words takes six lines). One row is taller than the screen.\n2. **Reader message header and body**: the body is indented by about 440 px of a 1206 px screen (avatar column), so the text runs at 3 to 5 words per line.\n3. **Topic list under a category**: the « Sous-forum » label is clipped by the top edge of its card; the picker value wraps onto two lines.\n4. **Favoris and topic rows**: the meta line truncates the last poster and drops the date (« name… », « name - il… »), and « 452 / 452 » wraps onto two lines.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- At accessibility sizes, each of the four places lays out on a stacked (vertical) arrangement instead of squeezing a column, with no clipped label and no truncated date.\n- A hosted test renders each place at `accessibility-extra-large` and checks the title column width (item 1) and the label frame inside its card (item 3).\n- Default size layouts do not change.\n\n### Sources\nScreenshots (pseudos blanked) are with the orchestrator, not attached here (no external hosting); issue #693 comment lists them. Related: #1170 (reader « + » ignores Dynamic Type), #572.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
